/-!
# The short exact sequences of Stacks 0DXW

Fix an algebraization situation: a Noetherian ring `A` with ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞`, the affine scheme
`X = Spec(A)` and the open complement `U = X ∖ V(𝔞)`. Let `(F_n)` be a coherent `I`-adic system
on `U`, and assume conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks 0DXW:

1. `I = (f)` is principal for a nonzerodivisor `f ∈ A`,
2. each `F_n` is a finite locally free `𝒪_U/f^n𝒪_U`-module.

This file derives from them the short exact sequences

  `0 → F_n → F_(n+1) → F_1 → 0`

that the proof of Stacks 0DXW uses, that is, condition (1) of Stacks 0H39 for multiplication by
`f`. This is the hypothesis `Stacks.Algebraization.HasPrincipalShortExactSequences` of
`Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_of_principal_shortExactSequences`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.scalarIdealData_mulBySection_eq_idealOnOpen` — for `I = (f)` the ideal
  sheaf `I 𝒪_U` is the ideal sheaf generated by the image of `f` in `Γ(U, 𝒪_U)`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_cokernelIso_systemMapSucc` — each transition map of the system
  presents its target as the cokernel of multiplication by `f ^ (n+1)`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_cokernelIso_proj` — the iterated transition `F_(n+1) ⟶ F_1`
  presents `F_1` as the cokernel of multiplication by `f`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isSMulRegular_baseToPointStalk` — a nonzerodivisor of `A` stays a
  nonzerodivisor in the local rings of `U`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.mem_pow_smul_stalk_of_smul_eq_zero` — the local content: an element of
  the stalk of `F_(n+1)` killed by `f` is an `f ^ (n+1)`-multiple.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.hasPrincipalShortExactSequences_of_locallyFree` — **the short exact
  sequences of the proof of Stacks 0DXW, from conditions (1) and (2) of that tag.**

## Implementation notes

The whole argument rests on one identification: for `I = (f)` the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf
`I 𝒪_U` coincides with `Stacks.Algebraization.scalarIdealData` of multiplication by the image of
`f`, i.e. with the ideal sheaf generated by that global section. The two are compared through
their stalks, each of which is `Ideal.span {f}` pushed into the local ring. Granted that,
`Stacks.Algebraization.principalPowerQuotientIso` turns every ideal-power quotient of the system
into a cokernel of multiplication by a power of `f`, and the two cokernel presentations above are
the clauses of the definition of a coherent adic system read in that form.

Condition (1) of Stacks 0H39 then asks for a map `ι : F_n ⟶ F_(n+1)` with `π ≫ ι = f` and for
`0 → F_n → F_(n+1) → F_1 → 0` to be short exact. The map is the descent of multiplication by `f`
along the first cokernel presentation, which exists because `F_(n+1)` is killed by `I ^ (n+2)`;
exactness at the middle and surjectivity are the second cokernel presentation, since a cokernel
presentation is unchanged by precomposition with an epimorphism
(`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_cokernelIso_of_epi_comp`). Injectivity of `ι` is the only place
where the hypotheses on `f` and on local freeness are used, and it is the one local step: `ι` is
injective on the stalk at `y` exactly when the `f`-torsion of the stalk of `F_(n+1)` lies in its
`f ^ (n+1)`-multiples, and that holds because the stalk is a free module over `𝒪_{U,y}/f^(n+2)`
and `f` is a nonzerodivisor of `𝒪_{U,y}`.

Monomorphy is transported from the `Stacks.ModuleSkyscraper.modulesStalkFunctor` spelling of the
stalk, in which the freeness result is stated, to the
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.stalkMap` spelling, in which monomorphy is detected; the two
have the same underlying function, both being determined by their action on germs
(`Stacks.Algebraization.stalkMap_apply_eq_modulesStalkFunctor_map_apply`).

Several compatibilities are assembled in term mode out of `Category.assoc` and `congrArg`: the
categories `Scheme.Modules` and `SheafOfModules` of a scheme carry separately declared instances,
and a goal mixing the two is not type-correct at the transparency a rewrite motive is built at.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H39](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H39)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EL6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EL6)
-/

